    "caption": "An ear wire is the wire that passes through the earlobe, and jewelers also call it a fish hook or French hook. Its end is open, so it can slip out when snagged, and a small rubber stopper can help hold it in place. The drop hangs from a small loop in the wire, and heavier drops often use a leverback, whose hinge snaps shut. Many ear wires are about 20 gauge, and nickel-free titanium wires suit people with sensitive ears. The renders in this video were made with HeyGema.",
